{"id":"03dcbc472c7a5883","group":"58","path":"58/batch06/58-df-kodaira-dimension.md","title":"Kodaira Dimension","display":"df-kodaira-dimension — Kodaira Dimension","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-kodaira-dimension","aliases":["58-df-kodaira-dimension"],"display":"df-kodaira-dimension — Kodaira Dimension","depends_on":["[[../batch02/58-df-canonical-bundle.md]]","[[../batch20/58-df-projective-variety.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-kodaira-dimension"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-kodaira-dimension</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-kodaira-dimension — Kodaira Dimension"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"369c9ce912d7ccb6\" href=\"?note=369c9ce912d7ccb6\" title=\"../batch02/58-df-canonical-bundle.md\">../batch02/58-df-canonical-bundle.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"6046552157f71d9c\" href=\"?note=6046552157f71d9c\" title=\"../batch20/58-df-projective-variety.md\">../batch20/58-df-projective-variety.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X,K_X,\\kappa\\in V\">\\(X,K_X,\\kappa\\in V\\)</span> (parameters)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{SmoothProjectiveVariety}_k(X)\">\\(\\operatorname{SmoothProjectiveVariety}_k(X)\\)</span> (smooth projective variety predicate)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"K_X\">\\(K_X\\)</span> (canonical divisor, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"369c9ce912d7ccb6\" href=\"?note=369c9ce912d7ccb6\" title=\"../batch02/58-df-canonical-bundle.md\">../batch02/58-df-canonical-bundle.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{KodairaDimension}_S\\subseteq V^3\">\\(\\mathrm{KodairaDimension}_S\\subseteq V^3\\)</span> (relation defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}kodaira\\text{-}dimension}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{KodairaDimension}_S(\\kappa,X,K_X)\\leftrightarrow\n\\operatorname{SmoothProjectiveVariety}_k(X)\\land\n\\left[\n\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\bigl(\\forall m\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;(h^0(X,mK_X)=0)\\land\\kappa=-\\infty\\bigr)\\\\\n&amp;{}\\lor\\Bigl(\\exists m\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;(h^0(X,mK_X)&gt;0)\\land\n\\kappa=\\max\\{\\dim\\Phi_{|mK_X|}(X)\\mid m\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\land h^0(X,mK_X)&gt;0\\}\\Bigr)\n\\end{aligned}\n\\right]\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}kodaira\\text{-}dimension}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{KodairaDimension}_S(\\kappa,X,K_X)\\leftrightarrow\n\\operatorname{SmoothProjectiveVariety}_k(X)\\land\n\\left[\n\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\bigl(\\forall m\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;(h^0(X,mK_X)=0)\\land\\kappa=-\\infty\\bigr)\\\\\n&amp;{}\\lor\\Bigl(\\exists m\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;(h^0(X,mK_X)&gt;0)\\land\n\\kappa=\\max\\{\\dim\\Phi_{|mK_X|}(X)\\mid m\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\land h^0(X,mK_X)&gt;0\\}\\Bigr)\n\\end{aligned}\n\\right]\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa(X) \\in \\{-\\infty, 0, 1, \\ldots, \\dim X\\}\">\\(\\kappa(X) \\in \\{-\\infty, 0, 1, \\ldots, \\dim X\\}\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa = \\dim X\">\\(\\kappa = \\dim X\\)</span>: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X\">\\(X\\)</span> is of general type.</li>\n<li>Calabi–Yau 簇和阿贝尔簇是 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa=0\">\\(\\kappa=0\\)</span> 的重要例子；该值不反向刻画这两类簇。</li>\n<li>Iitaka fibration: base of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"|mK_X|\">\\(|mK_X|\\)</span> for large <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"m\">\\(m\\)</span> has dimension <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch02/58-df-canonical-bundle.md","status":"resolved","id":"369c9ce912d7ccb6","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch02/58-df-canonical-bundle.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch20/58-df-projective-variety.md","status":"resolved","id":"6046552157f71d9c","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch20/58-df-projective-variety.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch02/58-df-canonical-bundle.md","status":"resolved","id":"369c9ce912d7ccb6","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$K_X$ (canonical divisor, see [[../batch02/58-df-canonical-bundle.md]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"X,K_X,\\kappa\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{SmoothProjectiveVariety}_k(X)","display":false},{"tex":"K_X","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{KodairaDimension}_S\\subseteq V^3","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}kodaira\\text{-}dimension}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{KodairaDimension}_S(\\kappa,X,K_X)\\leftrightarrow\n\\operatorname{SmoothProjectiveVariety}_k(X)\\land\n\\left[\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\bigl(\\forall m\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;(h^0(X,mK_X)=0)\\land\\kappa=-\\infty\\bigr)\\\\\n&{}\\lor\\Bigl(\\exists m\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;(h^0(X,mK_X)>0)\\land\n\\kappa=\\max\\{\\dim\\Phi_{|mK_X|}(X)\\mid m\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\land h^0(X,mK_X)>0\\}\\Bigr)\n\\end{aligned}\n\\right]","display":true},{"tex":"\\kappa(X) \\in \\{-\\infty, 0, 1, \\ldots, \\dim X\\}","display":false},{"t